From eab4b09f902d569513cba462bad90c8343b849e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:02:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Call last_frame last_in_image and say what it ends

This commit renames the key last_frame of the started event to
last_in_image. It is true on the last frame of the image that the
application combines, not on the last frame of the scan: a feeder has
more pages, and so more images, after it. The old name suggested the
end of everything.

The documentation of StartFrame() now says that the passes red, green
and blue are values of the format key of the started event, that
last_in_image completes one image, and that a feeder scan continues
with the next page until a no-documents event. It also uses "handheld"
for the scanners the capability handheld names.

Tested with the scenario checks, which pass. The hardware cancel script
reads the new key and was not run, and no multi-pass scanner was tried.
---
 data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml | 24 +++++++++++++++---------
 src/scanner-helper.c                    |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml b/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
index 6681510..bdbc730 100644
--- a/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
+++ b/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
@@ -17,7 +17,9 @@
       a list of typed options, and image data delivered one frame at a time.
 
       Typical use: SelectScanners() once, OpenScanner(), GetOptions(),
-      SetOptions(), then StartFrame() until last_frame is true.
+      SetOptions(), then StartFrame() until last_in_image is true, which
+      completes one image. A feeder scan is one image per page: call
+      StartFrame() again for the next, until a ``no-documents`` event.
 
       An application finds out whether the portal can be used by checking
       that the ``version`` property of this interface exists on
@@ -398,15 +400,19 @@
           A 16-bit sample is two bytes in the host's byte order, as SANE
           delivers it. Samples of one pixel are next to each other in a row.
 
-        * A scan in several passes is several frames, one for each of
-          ``red``, ``green`` and ``blue``, and ``last_frame`` is true on the
-          last of them. The application combines them.
+        * An image can take several frames. A scan in several passes is one
+          frame for each of the ``format`` values ``red``, ``green`` and
+          ``blue``, and the application combines them into one image.
+          ``last_in_image`` in the ``started`` event is true on the last frame
+          of the image. It is not the end of the scan: a feeder has another
+          page, and so another image, after it.
 
         * When ``lines`` is -1 the height is not known in advance, as for a
-          hand scanner, and the frame is as long as the data on the pipe.
+          handheld scanner, and the frame is as long as the data on the pipe.
 
-        Call again after ``finished`` while ``last_frame`` was false (for
-        example separate red, green, blue and infrared frames). Fails with
+        Call again after ``finished`` while ``last_in_image`` was false, for
+        the next frame of the same image (for example separate red, green,
+        blue and infrared frames). Fails with
         ``org.freedesktop.portal.Error.Busy`` if a frame is in progress.
         Closing the pipe early cancels the frame, as does Cancel().
 
@@ -458,8 +464,8 @@
         ``format`` (``s``: ``gray``, ``rgb``, ``red``, ``green``, ``blue``, and for
         scanners with an infrared channel ``ir``, ``rgbi``, ``grayi``),
         ``depth`` (``u``), ``pixels_per_line`` (``u``), ``bytes_per_line``
-        (``u``), ``lines`` (``i``, -1 when unknown, as for hand scanners)
-        and ``last_frame`` (``b``).
+        (``u``), ``lines`` (``i``, -1 when unknown, as for handheld scanners)
+        and ``last_in_image`` (``b``).
 
         ``finished``: all data was written. ``cancelled``: the frame was
         cancelled. ``no-documents``: the feeder or film holder is empty or
diff --git a/src/scanner-helper.c b/src/scanner-helper.c
index 50c2da4..0cbc072 100644
--- a/src/scanner-helper.c
+++ b/src/scanner-helper.c
@@ -771,7 +771,7 @@ frame_parameters_to_variant (const SANE_Parameters *params,
   g_variant_builder_add (&builder, "{sv}", "pixels_per_line", g_variant_new_uint32 (params->pixels_per_line));
   g_variant_builder_add (&builder, "{sv}", "bytes_per_line", g_variant_new_uint32 (params->bytes_per_line));
   g_variant_builder_add (&builder, "{sv}", "lines", g_variant_new_int32 (params->lines));
-  g_variant_builder_add (&builder, "{sv}", "last_frame", g_variant_new_boolean (params->last_frame));
+  g_variant_builder_add (&builder, "{sv}", "last_in_image", g_variant_new_boolean (params->last_frame));
 
   return g_variant_builder_end (&builder);
 }
-- 
